       pcap-linktype - link-layer header types supported by libpcap

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       For  a  live  capture  or ``savefile'', libpcap supplies, as the return
       value of the ppccaapp__ddaattaalliinnkk(3) routine, a value that indicates the  type
       of link-layer header at the beginning of the packets it provides.  This
       is not necessarily the type of link-layer header that the packets being
       captured have on the network from which they're being captured; for ex‐
       ample, packets from an IEEE 802.11 network might be provided by libpcap
       with  Ethernet  headers that the network adapter or the network adapter
       driver generates from the 802.11 headers.  The names for  those  values
       begin with DDLLTT__, so they are sometimes called "DLT_ values".

       The  values  stored in the link-layer header type field in the savefile
       header are, in most but not all cases, the same as the values  returned
       by ppccaapp__ddaattaalliinnkk().  The names for those values begin with LLIINNKKTTYYPPEE__.

       The  link-layer  header  types  supported  by  libpcap are described at
       https://www.tcpdump.org/linktypes.html .

